      "writtenOn": "2023-03-28T02:24:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "without this, the gcc linker for the unittest build would not be able to link the library:\n```\n/usr/bin/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-ar: crypto/fipsmodule/CMakeFiles/fipsmodule.dir/bcm.c.o: plugin needed to handle lto object\n/usr/bin/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-ranlib: crypto/libcrypto.a(bcm.c.o): plugin needed to handle lto object\n  EXE     fpsensor_state.exe\n/usr/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu/binutils-bin/2.36.1/ld.bfd.real: build/host/fpsensor_state/RO/common/fpsensor/fpsensor_crypto.o: in function `aes_gcm_encrypt\u0027:\n/mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/common/fpsensor/fpsensor_crypto.cc:255: undefined reference to `AES_set_encrypt_key\u0027\n/usr/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu/binutils-bin/2.36.1/ld.bfd.real: build/host/fpsensor_state/RO/common/fpsensor/fpsensor_crypto.o: in function `aes_gcm_encrypt\u0027:\n/mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/third_party/boringssl/include/aes_gcm_helpers.h:32: undefined reference to `AES_encrypt\u0027\n...\n```\n\nAnd we already add the correct `CMAKE_SYSROOT`:\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3925087/44/third_party/rules.mk#55",
      "parentUuid": "398905c0_ec383f38",
      "range": {
