        "id": 1293547
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-29T04:48:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Changing the CMAKE_LINKER does not work for the boringssl static library case.\nBecause there is no \"linker\" stage when we generate the \"static library\".\n\nThe problem is the `ar,nm,ranlib` would not work with the \".o\" files that were compiled with \"gcc -flto\". And they will drop the \".o\" files that they cannot handle from the static library archive(\".a\").\n\nThe only way to let them handle the \".o\" files correctly is using the `gcc-ar,gcc-nm,gcc-ranlib` to archive the \".o\" files to \".a\".\n\n------\n\nBTW, the place that linking the static lib into the binary is here:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/Makefile.rules;drc\u003da6505051ba9d893f71738acdb3e242fb37b90426;l\u003d101\n\nAnd I don\u0027t want to refactor the whole EC toolchain...",
